{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "שפה יהי' לפיו", :translit "sfah yihyeh lo-fi", :gloss "a mouth it shall have for its opening"} {:he "שהמעיל מכפר על לשה\"ר", :translit "sheha-me'il mechaper al lashon ha-ra", :gloss "that the me'il atones for evil speech"} {:he "שפה לפיו", :translit "sfah le-fiv", :gloss "a mouth for his mouth"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Wordplay linking the garment's 'mouth' (שפה) to guarding one's own mouth from lashon ha-ra."}], :frame {:text "Each priestly garment atones for a specific category of sin. The me'il atones for lashon ha-ra, as taught in Arakhin 16a, and the Psikta Rabbati section on parashat Tetzaveh lists the atonement each garment provides. The verse 'It shall have a mouth' (Exodus 28:32) is read as an allusion to this atonement: just as the garment has a mouth, so one who misused speech must guard his mouth, refrain from lashon ha-ra, and repent.", :sources ["Arakhin 16a" "Exodus 28:32" "Psikta Rabbati 14 (Tetzaveh)"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Wordplay linking the garment's 'mouth' (שפה) to guarding one's own mouth from lashon ha-ra.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:19:55.910312721Z", :model "glm-5.2"}